    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.files\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nCurrently, mini.files opens at the top. But when opening small files most of the content is obscured until mini.files is closed. It's also far from the command line at the bottom of the window, where I use a user command to open mini.files.\r\n\r\nI'd love an option to open mini.files at the bottom of the window.  \r\n- It wouldn't obscure small files opened with mini.files  \r\n- I wouldn't need to move my eyes very far at all after typing my user command to open mini.files",
